---
layout: null
permalink: /feed.xml
sitemap: false
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"{% if site.lang %} xml:lang="{{ site.lang }}"{% endif %}>
  <generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="{{ jekyll.version }}">Jekyll</generator>
  <link href="{{ page.url | absolute_url }}" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml" />
  <link href="{{ '/' | absolute_url }}" rel="alternate" type="text/html"{% if site.lang %} hreflang="{{ site.lang }}"{% endif %} />
  <updated>{{ site.time | date_to_xmlschema }}</updated>
  <id>{{ page.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</id>
  <title type="html">{{ site.title | default: site.name | smartify | xml_escape }}</title>
  {% if site.description %}
  <subtitle>{{ site.description | xml_escape }}</subtitle>
  {% endif %}
  {% if site.author %}
  <author>
    <name>{{ site.author.name | default: site.author | xml_escape }}</name>
  </author>
  {% endif %}
  {%- comment -%}
  Ce dépôt n'utilise pas les "posts" Jekyll (pas de _posts/) : ce flux personnalisé remplace le
  flux par défaut de jekyll-feed (vide, car basé sur site.posts) en listant les fiches par date de
  dernière revue factuelle (last_factual_review), le signal de fraîcheur réel de ce projet.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% assign entries = site.pages | where_exp: "p", "p.last_factual_review" | sort: "last_factual_review" | reverse %}
  {% for entry in entries limit: 30 %}
  <entry>
    {% assign entry_title = entry.title | smartify | strip_html | normalize_whitespace %}
    <title type="html">{{ entry_title }}</title>
    <link href="{{ entry.url | absolute_url }}" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="{{ entry_title }}" />
    <published>{{ entry.last_factual_review | date_to_xmlschema }}</published>
    <updated>{{ entry.last_factual_review | date_to_xmlschema }}</updated>
    <id>{{ entry.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</id>
    {% if entry.description %}
    <summary type="html"><![CDATA[{{ entry.description | strip_html | normalize_whitespace }}]]></summary>
    {% endif %}
  </entry>
  {% endfor %}
</feed>
